## Context

The arena's quality axis rests on a 3-seat panel (gemini / grok /
minimax, one rubric, lineage-decorrelated). Unanswered: how sensitive
are the cycle conclusions to one seat?

## Scope

- Leave-one-judge-out analysis on the complete cycle-1+2 data
  (~420 seat verdicts, all in ~/arena/runs/*/judges/): recompute the
  grid, the paired verdicts (H1/H2, effort axes, cross-camp) and the
  cluster table with each seat removed, and with all pairs.
- Identify: does ANY single seat's removal flip a conclusion? Which
  seat is most load-bearing? Which is most divergent (and is the
  divergence systematic — e.g., a leniency bias, as suspected in the
  2026-10-05 panel-comparison of gemini-flash)?
- If one seat is dispensable, the panel cost drops by a third.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Leave-one-out recomputation scripted (reproducible, not hand-work)
- [ ] Per-conclusion stability table: which verdicts flip, which hold
- [ ] Verdict recorded: panel composition recommendation for cycle 3
